; REQUEST-09: a dep whose own spec produces a collapsed-set shape through ANONYMOUS generic
; instances at field sites (`set<key_hash>` / `nonempty_set<key_hash>`), NOT a named rule. The
; synthesized instance wasm wrapper lowers to the STRUCTURAL name (`KeyHashList` /
; `NonEmptyKeyHashList`), exactly like the inline `[* key_hash]` / `[+ key_hash]` equivalent — so a
; consumer's `--wrapper-requests` for that structural shape is satisfied by own-spec (no criterion-8
; #3 hard error on the synthesized name), and the two spellings are ONE wasm class.
;
; The generic defs carry the explicit `; @duplicates preserve` opt-out: tag 258 now defaults to
; `@duplicates reject` (the well-known-tag registry), which would swap the plain `Vec`/structural-list
; wrapper for the `OrderedSet` twin and break the structural convergence this REQUEST-09 fixture pins.
; The convergence machinery under test is orthogonal to the duplicates policy, so it stays on the
; plain representation via the opt-out.
key_hash = bytes ; @newtype
set<a0> = #6.258([* a0]) / [* a0] ; @duplicates preserve
nonempty_set<a0> = #6.258([+ a0]) / [+ a0] ; @duplicates preserve
cert = [pool_owners: set<key_hash>, extra: [* key_hash]]
signers = [required: nonempty_set<key_hash>]
